(h) The Department may adopt rules to implement the changes made by this amendatory Act of the 102nd General Assembly.
(Source: P.A. 102-1117, eff. 1-13-23; 103-1048, eff. 1-1-25.)

(405 ILCS 5/3-911)
Sec. 3-911. Aftercare plan.
(a) The Department of Human Services when a recipient of services under this Code, whether admitted on a voluntary or involuntary basis, is being discharged from an inpatient facility, shall provide  the  recipient and the recipient's conservator, guardian, or other legally authorized representative a written aftercare plan prior to the recipient's discharge from the facility.
 The written aftercare plan shall include, to the extent known, all of the following components:
